text.section:
Each bulk user of alternative fuel and retailer of alternative fuel shall file a monthly informational return with the Commissioner. A monthly return covers a calendar month and is due by the twentieth day of the second month that follows such month.
			The return shall include the following information and any other information required by the Commissioner:

The amount of alternative fuel received during the month;


The amount of alternative fuel sold or used during the month;


The number of gallons for which a deduction was taken during the month pursuant to § 58.1-2254, by provider, if applicable; and


The number of gallons sold in exempt sales during the month, by type of sale, and the purchaser of the fuel in the exempt sales, if applicable.
